# What ships to consumers, versus what stays in the repository.
#
# This library is installed into a WordPress plugin's vendor/ directory, which is
# web-reachable on most hosts. Until v1.3.2 it shipped tests/run.php, and an
# anonymous GET to it on a live site executed the whole suite and returned 200.
# Archives are what Composer installs from — GitHub's and GitLab's zipball
# endpoints both honour export-ignore — so pruning here is what keeps every
# consumer clean on its next `composer update`, including consumers nobody has
# written yet. Doing it in each consumer's build script instead would be a thing
# to remember forever, in every repo.
#
# NOTE export-ignore applies to ARCHIVES, not to clones: `composer install
# --prefer-source` clones and would still fetch tests/. That is why tests/run.php
# ALSO refuses to run outside the CLI. The two together cover both paths; neither
# covers both alone.
/tests          export-ignore
/README.md      export-ignore
/CHANGELOG.md   export-ignore
/.gitignore     export-ignore
/.gitattributes export-ignore
